_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State in the plan why the RAM disk is chosen over disabling Git fsync in the test stores (core.fsync=none / GIT_TEST_FSYNC=0), which targets the same profiled git-commit cost with lower blast radius — or adopt the simpler approach if it is comparable.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Context: 'cProfile attributes 13.69s to 24 required git-add/git-commit pairs'","src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:508 run_git_write drives real `git` subprocess commit/add ops that fsync","search 'core.fsync' -> (no matches): no fsync-tuning alternative is referenced anywhere","ABSENCE: plan proposes only the storage-layer RAM disk; no config-layer option weighed"],"finding":"The plan does not consider a structurally-simpler, lower-blast-radius alternative that attacks the same named cost: disabling Git fsync durability in the throwaway test stores (e.g. core.fsync=none / GIT_TEST_FSYNC=0). The profiled long pole is 24 git-add/git-commit pairs whose system-CPU cost is largely fsync; the suite issues real `git` subprocesses (src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:run_git_write), so a test-environment fsync-off config would take effect and avoid the RAM-disk device lifecycle (create/detach/cleanup, memory-pressure cap, mount-path resolution) entirely.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5988ab2846d2ac6f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan §Context and evidence / §Plan step 3","norm_id":"n89b653fe6216dfeb","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["macOS matrix cell where fsync-off would cut the same 13.69s without a RAM disk","future runner-image change that breaks hdiutil/APFS tooling but not a git config"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a one-sentence positive rationale distinguishing the RAM disk from a fsync-off config (e.g. 'fsync-off changes git durability semantics under test and does not cover non-git small-write cost; the RAM disk keeps every git op byte-identical'), or adopt the fsync approach if measurement shows it is at-least-as-good.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the RAM disk is sized against the PEAK single-tier retained footprint (the larger of the default vs integration basetemp), since the two tiers sequentially reuse one volume, then apply the >=50% headroom and <40%-physical bounds.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.599,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 2: 'Measure retained temp allocated bytes and file count ... using the same selectors and distinct explicit basetemps. Size the RAM disk with at least 50% headroom'","Impl comment lines 721-724: 'The tiers are sequential ... Release only its exact basetemp after a successful default run so integration can reuse the 2 GiB volume.'"],"finding":"Step 2's sizing input is ambiguous given the sequential single-volume design. The two tiers reuse ONE RAM disk (default basetemp released before integration), so the sizing driver must be the PEAK single-tier retained footprint (the larger of default vs integration), not their sum or an unqualified aggregate. The plan says to measure 'retained temp allocated bytes ... using the same selectors and distinct explicit basetemps' without stating that the RAM disk is sized against the larger single tier.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f39458ecd4abf750e","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan §Plan step 2; step 4 ('measured default tree is larger than 1 GiB')","norm_id":"n2a3c4a1d20e290be","priority":0.201,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader sizes against the SUM of both tiers' retained bytes and over-allocates toward the 40% cap, or sizes against only one tier and under-provisions the larger tier"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{